project, and its use of them does not imply FINOS's endorsement.

The framework cites other publishers' works
-------------------------------------------

FINOS's reference files, under docs/_data/references/, name other publishers' works.
Each work keeps its owner's rights, and FINOS's CC-BY-4.0 covers FINOS's files, not
those works. This project's catalogue names each entry by FINOS's key alone. An SSSOM
set carries an entry's title as its label only where the cited work's terms, read on
2026-11-05, allow a copy of the entry's name; LABEL_POSITIONS in
scripts/build_sssom_mappings.py records the position for each file, and a test holds
every file to one. No set carries an entry's description.

- Carried: atr (MIT); ffiec-itbooklets, nist-ai-600-1, nist-sp-800-53r5 and sr11-7
  (United States government works, 17 U.S.C. 105); eu-ai-act (the regulation's
  article headings, which the Commission's Decision 2011/833/EU leaves free to
  reuse); owasp-asi, owasp-llm and owasp-ml (CC BY-SA 4.0, the entries' names, with
  OWASP named as the source in this notice and the file's address in each row);
  canada-regulations and uk-regulations (the names of Crown and regulators'
  documents, as FINOS cites them).
- Not carried: iso-42001, whose titles may be ISO's headings, and
  iosco-supervisory-toolkit, whose terms could not be read, since IOSCO's site
  refuses scripts. A citation of an ISO standard by number gives no right to its
  text, and no ISO publication was read in making this project.

